                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Rotation through 180°: ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "y=\\frac{1-x}{2x+1}",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p19-q41-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Replace the relevant coordinate signs; a 180° rotation replaces both.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Reflection in the $x$-axis: replace $y$ by $-y$.\n$$\\begin{align*}-y&=\\frac{x+1}{2x-1}\\\\y&=\\frac{x+1}{1-2x}\\end{align*}$$\nReflection in the $y$-axis: replace $x$ by $-x$.\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{-x+1}{-2x-1}\\\\y&=\\frac{x-1}{2x+1}\\end{align*}$$\nRotation through $180^\\circ$ about the origin: replace both $x$ and $y$ by their negatives.\n$$\\begin{align*}-y&=\\frac{-x+1}{-2x-1}\\\\-y&=\\frac{x-1}{2x+1}\\\\y&=\\frac{1-x}{2x+1}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 122
      },
