                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Reflection in the $x$-axis:\n$$\\begin{align*}-y&=\\sin x+\\cos x\\\\y&=-\\sin x-\\cos x\\end{align*}$$\nUse $\\sin(-x)=-\\sin x$ and $\\cos(-x)=\\cos x$ for the remaining substitutions.\nReflection in the $y$-axis:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\sin(-x)+\\cos(-x)\\\\y&=-\\sin x+\\cos x\\end{align*}$$\nRotation through $180^\\circ$ about the origin:\n$$\\begin{align*}-y&=\\sin(-x)+\\cos(-x)\\\\-y&=-\\sin x+\\cos x\\\\y&=\\sin x-\\cos x\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
